---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'

const images = [
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-117/01-the-orbital-strike.png",
    "title": "The Orbital Strike",
    "caption": "Epic wide shot: a colossal beam of radiant light arcs across a sunless alien sky, refracting through a chain of floating crystal mirrors in orbit, and slams down onto the lip of a vast cavern pit. The earth splits in glowing cracks."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-117/02-the-popcorn-scene.png",
    "title": "The Popcorn Scene",
    "caption": "Inside a perfectly smooth, cylindrical stone bore in an alien mountain, a gaunt mind flayer in tattered robes hunches over the putrefying corpse of another mind flayer, tentacles buried in its opened skull, eating its brain. Behind him, an immense alien machine of glowing crystals and impossible gears."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-117/03-qdv-on-the-laser-throne.png",
    "title": "QDV on the Laser Throne",
    "caption": "A lone mind flayer strapped into a throne at the heart of a colossal alien laser machine, a crown of electrodes and diodes lowered onto his bulbous skull, at night. Rage smolders in his white eyes, and his anger is reflected and glittering in hundreds of jewels and crystals in the machine around him."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-117/04-bahamut-purifies-the-eggs.png",
    "title": "Bahamut Purifies the Eggs",
    "caption": "Inside a ruined temple, a small Kobold paladin kneels amid the scattered, age-worn stones of a shattered platinum dragon statue. A Light cantrip above his head has flared into blinding silver brilliance, and a single silver ray lances down onto two petrified dragon eggs."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-117/05-a-hangnail-of-reality.png",
    "title": "A Hangnail of Reality",
    "caption": "A Dragonborn fighter on a desolate gray mountainside holds a jagged, geometric crystalline shard that has cut a fist-sized tear into the air itself. The tear is raw and fleshlike at the edges, a hangnail of reality peeled back, and through it snow and cold wind blow in from a steampunk industrial world of smokestacks and gaslight."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-117/06-heroes-feast-on-a-dead-world.png",
    "title": "Heroes' Feast on a Dead World",
    "caption": "Wide shot: on cracked, irradiated gray ground under a sunless sky with yellow-and-purple poisoned rivers, a lush, impossible feast has appeared, conjured by a druid. There are vibrant fruits, roots, bread, greenery, and flowers, the only color in the landscape."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-117/07-the-carpet-snatch.png",
    "title": "The Carpet Snatch",
    "caption": "Mid-air, fifty feet above a cracked and glowing battlefield: an elder-brain dragon hybrid seizes a flying carpet in both claws, tentacles lashing from its face. A Dragonborn fighter and a druid tumble off the carpet into open air, and the druid is mid-transformation into a giant vulture, feathers bursting from his robes."
  },
  {
    "src": "/studio/session-117/08-the-trip.png",
    "title": "The Trip",
    "caption": "Low angle: a winged Dragonborn fighter, exhausted after a string of missed swings, finally connects a sword strike that sends a gargantuan elder-brain dragon crashing out of the sky into cracked earth, with a shockwave of dust and debris. On the ground, the dragon twists its tentacled head upward toward the fighter, its maw opening, and a swarm of glistening illithid tadpoles is about to spray out."
  }
]
---

<Layout title="Session 117 — Tales of the Radiant Citadel" description="With the God Brain dead, the party turned on the second Elder Brain: the High Master. Erik played QDV, a dumb mind flayer, for the night. QDV found the god">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
    <a href="/studio" class="text-sm text-earth hover:text-ink transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">&larr; Studio</a>

    <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black leading-tight mb-2">
      Session 117
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-earth mb-1">Tales of the Radiant Citadel &middot; October 13, 2026</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-light mb-8">Bluetspur Expedition (Finale, Part 1)</p>

    <div class="prose-section text-ink-light leading-relaxed mb-12 space-y-4">
      <p>
        With the God Brain dead, the party turned on the second Elder Brain: the High Master. Erik played QDV, a dumb mind flayer, for the night. QDV found the god-faction's orbital space laser, ate a dead flayer's brain to learn how to fire it, and learned he had been the hive's laughingstock. Haru reconsecrated a ruined shrine and rolled a nat 20, and Bahamut purified the Elder Brain Dragon eggs into two silver dragon eggs. Haru then lured the High Master out of his pit. QDV's first shot hit the dragon for 116 radiant, but it also cracked the earth, downed Haru, and dealt 58 to most of the party. The session ends mid-combat: Kiet has tripped the bloodied High Master out of the sky, and it is about to breathe tadpoles at him.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Highlights</h2>
    <ul class="text-sm text-ink-light leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-12 list-disc list-inside">
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Pre-Game: The Gordian Trailer</strong> — The table praised Erik's AI video intro for his next character. Hunter: *&quot;It is a good time capsule... Eric is doing videos. We'll have to start adding into this.&quot;* Another player: *&quot;A fully, a fully realized AI video intro.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Sam's Opener: The Four Tribes</strong> — Sam: *&quot;To kill a mind flayer leader, a being that regards itself as a god, is no small feat. And now you've set your sights on a second one. The Highmaster, that dragon-elder brain hybrid, awaits in its lair, preparing to launch... a mission across the cosmos to reconnect with the whole of the Illithid diaspora, perhaps subjugating other worlds in that process.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Twelve Dissents</strong> — Twelve, the cranium rat, asks Kiet why they're killing the High Master: *&quot;But we do need a leader, and if you kill the other leader on this planet... There will be no one to lead us... What worthy mind flayer will you find?&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Space Laser</strong> — The beam that shot down the party's ship came from the western mountains. QDV's Arcana check says he knows where the laser is. His old job there: *&quot;Polishing the lens.&quot;* Sam: *&quot;Absolutely. That would be about what the task is.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">QDV Eats a Brain (The Popcorn Scene)</strong> — Erik: *&quot;I might go try to eat, you know, Uncle Ned or Steve.&quot;* Sam: the brains are 16 hours old and unpickled. Erik: &quot;We're recyclers in my family, what can I say?&quot;</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Concept of a Plan</strong> — The plan: Haru lures the High Master out with flattery, QDV fires on the signal, Toven and Kiet drop dynamite from the carpet, and Gemnar ambushes.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Gemnar's Prophecy (Radburn Shrapnel)</strong> — A sack-skinned seer: *&quot;I've studied these Woodland Rollers. I know their destiny. You don't exist as far as the histories go. What is your destiny, Gemnar?&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Can This World Heal?</strong> — A mutant to Toven: *&quot;Our water is yellow and purple in some places. Those are probably not colors that water should be.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Bahamut Purifies the Eggs (Broken Glare)</strong> — The ruined city once held perhaps 100,000 people; a couple hundred mutants remain. Bahamut's statue lies scattered as worn stones.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Kiet Tests the Universe Knife</strong> — Kiet borrows the carpet. Erik: *&quot;Hey Dad, can I borrow the car?&quot;* / *&quot;Make sure to fuel it up when you bring it home.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Eve of Battle</strong> — Gemnar recruits brutes. One brute: *&quot;We have spent generations in cowardice... and now you tell us that we should fight for ourselves?&quot;* / Gemnar: *&quot;If you're a coward, then don't.&quot;* / Sam: &quot;There is an ancient battle cry that I have heard of. It is 3 words. Let's fucking go.&quot; Three translucent brutes join him.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Lure</strong> — Sam: *&quot;There is a pit... a vast cavern, protrusions from the walls like teeth, illithids hanging below like bats.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">The Orbital Strike — 116 Radiant From Orbit</strong> — QDV calls down the god-faction's orbital laser on Haru's signal: 20d10 = 116 radiant straight into the High Master. The earth cracks, the back row of mind flayers is vaporized, and Haru and most of the party get hit too.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Round 1</strong> — Kiet: drops dynamite from the carpet, still a failure after Tactical Mind, and the cracked ground shakes harder. Sam: *&quot;Half of 30 is 19.&quot;*</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink">Kiet's Catastrophic, Triumphant Turn</strong> — Wings, flight, Action Surge. The scimitar hits, but the vicious short sword misses on 2, 3, 5, 2, and two Precision Attack dice are wasted. Sam: *&quot;Oh my fucking God, the odds of this are so low.&quot;*</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Art</h2>
    <div class="space-y-10">
      {images.map((img) => (
        <figure>
          <img
            src={img.src}
            alt={img.title}
            class="w-full rounded-xl shadow-lg"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-3">
            <span class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm">{img.title}</span>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-light mt-1">{img.caption}</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="border-t border-cream-dark mt-16 pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold mb-3">Party</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">QDV (temp)</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Erik)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Kiet</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Jonas)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Virgil Gemnar</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Kyle)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Toven</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Max)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Haru</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Hunter)</span></div>
        <div><span class="font-semibold text-ink">DM</span> <span class="text-ink-light">(Sam)</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
